    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d678">

                <pb facs="0791" n="671" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg671"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Gummeré to Acting Secretary of State
                        Adee.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-08-01"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 1, 1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 38.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to report that I have been informed
                    by the Portuguese minister that his government has accepted the invitation to
                    take part in the proposed Morocco conference. The only goverment remaining to be
                    heard from is that of Norway and Sweden.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">S. R. Gummeré.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
